Verizon has apologized to customers who pre-ordered the iPhone Duo through the carrier but have since been informed that their delivery is delayed.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Verizon-iPhone-Duo.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072755" /><br/>
In an email sent to affected customers, Verizon said an "unexpected shipping delay" means that iPhone Duo deliveries to some customers will "take a little longer." To make up for the inconvenience, Verizon is offering affected customers a &#36;100 Verizon gift card that can be used online or in-store toward bill payments or merchandise.<br/>
<br/>
"We owe you an apology," said Verizon. "We appreciate your patience and the opportunity to make this right," the company added.<br/>
<br/>
Verizon said customers will receive an email about the &#36;100 gift card next week, and it assured that it is working to fulfill orders as soon as it can.<br/>
<br/>
"Your order is secure, your place in line hasn't changed, and our team is actively tracking your shipment to get it to you as quickly as possible," said Verizon.<br/>
<br/>
<em>MacRumors</em> reader Ryan showed us that he pre-ordered an iPhone Duo from Verizon when pre-orders began on Friday, October 16. Verizon initially quoted him a Friday, October 23 delivery date, meaning he would have received the device on its launch day, but his estimated delivery date has since been revised to Saturday, November 7.<br/>
<br/>
There are many similar examples of Verizon customers with delayed pre-orders <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/verizon-order-status-iphone-duo.2491898/page-17">across the MacRumors Forums</a>, <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/verizon/comments/1xdrj79/just_got_this_from_verizon_regarding_late/">Reddit</a>, and other social media platforms, with many revised delivery dates now falling in the October 31 to November 14 window.<br/>
<br/>
Some customers who pre-ordered an iPhone Duo through Verizon did receive the device on October 23, so not everyone is impacted.<br/>
<br/>
Last week, Apple said pre-order demand for the iPhone Duo was "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/apple-iphone-duo-demand-extraordinary/">nothing short of extraordinary</a>," with estimated delivery dates on its own online store <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/iphone-duo-preorder-shipping-wait-times/">pushing into late January</a> for new orders. Some lucky customers managed to secure an iPhone Duo <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-long-lines-at-apple-stores/">on a walk-in basis</a> yesterday, while in-store pickup reservations <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/24/apple-store-pickup-iphone-duo-us/">resumed with little to no availability</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Leading up to the iPhone Duo launch, there were a few reports mentioning that there would be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/11/iphone-duo-retail-showcase/">supply constraints</a> due to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/29/iphone-duo-reportedly-facing-production-problems/">alleged manufacturing challenges</a>. In any case, getting the device early is proving to be a challenge for some.<br/>
<br/>
